GHOST_GAINS — route the merkle-node double-SHA (TransformD64) through the accelerated Transform.

⛔ EXPERIMENTAL, OPT-IN, AND IT MOVES METHOD_ID. Applied only when HAZYNC_SHA_D64_ACCEL=1.
⚠ Applies ON TOP of patches/0002, which is what makes sha256::Transform the risc0 accelerator.

patches/0002 accelerates Transform and mentions TransformD64 only as a CONTEXT line. They are
different functions: TransformD64 is Core's fully-unrolled double-SHA over 64 bytes, used for EVERY
merkle tree node, and it still ran entirely in software. patches/0009's fast path does not touch it
either.

MEASURED on the production aggregate after the read_slice fix: sha256::TransformD64 is 124,759,624
cycles, 15.41% of the aggregate and its second-largest term.

This is one line, and it is Core's OWN idiom. Core ships TransformD64Wrapper<tr> precisely so that a
platform with a fast Transform can reuse it for the D64 path, and sets exactly this on SHA-NI, SSE4
and ARM SHA-NI:

    TransformD64 = TransformD64Wrapper<sha256_x86_shani::Transform>;
    TransformD64 = TransformD64Wrapper<sha256_sse4::Transform>;

We are doing the same with the accelerator as the underlying Transform. No new cryptography, no
consensus change, and Core's own SelfTest() validates the result -- the same self-test that guards
every other platform-specific Transform Core ships.

--- a/src/crypto/sha256.cpp
+++ b/src/crypto/sha256.cpp
@@ -413,7 +413,16 @@
 }
 
 TransformType Transform = sha256::Transform;
+#ifdef HAZYNC_SHA_D64_ACCEL
+/* Route the merkle-node double-SHA through the ACCELERATED Transform, using Core's own generic
+ * construction. This is exactly what Core does on any platform with a fast Transform -- see the
+ * SHA-NI, SSE4 and ARM branches below, all of which set TransformD64Wrapper<that Transform>.
+ * patches/0002 already made sha256::Transform the risc0 accelerator, so this points the D64 path at
+ * it too. No new cryptography, and SelfTest() checks the result. */
+TransformD64Type TransformD64 = TransformD64Wrapper<sha256::Transform>;
+#else
 TransformD64Type TransformD64 = sha256::TransformD64;
+#endif
 TransformD64Type TransformD64_2way = nullptr;
 TransformD64Type TransformD64_4way = nullptr;
 TransformD64Type TransformD64_8way = nullptr;
